# "You" in Null Summoner's threshold ability is its controller (CR 109.5), asked of whoever controls it now (CR 611.3a): its
# graveyard is the one counted, and that player may cast the exiled card. Bot1's Summoner exiles Bot2's Lightning Bolt and Bot1
# mills itself to twenty cards. On turn two Bot2 takes the Summoner with Act of Treason: with two cards in its own graveyard
# and its Mountain, Mox Sapphire and Mox Ruby open, Bot2 can't cast the Bolt yet - Bot1's threshold is not its controller's.
# Bot2 mills itself to eighteen with Brain Freeze. Now Bot1, with threshold and Mox Pearl open, can't cast the Bolt: the Summoner is not its own. Bot2 can, its own
# card, by the ability of the creature it controls, and with its own threshold - the Bolt hits Bot1.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Black Lotus
Mox Jet
Null Summoner
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Brain Freeze
Island x30

[Bot2 Deck]
